    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Express $x^2$ in the form:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p19-q7-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$A(x+1)^2+B(x+1)+C$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x+1)^2-2(x+1)+1$",
          "worked": "Equating coefficients of $x^2$ gives $A=1$. Substitute $x=-1$ to obtain $C$, then $x=0$ to obtain $B$.\n$$\\begin{align*}C&=(-1)^2\\\\C&=1\\\\0&=1+B+1\\\\B&=-2\\\\x^2&=(x+1)^2-2(x+1)+1\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p19-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$A(x-4)^2+B(x-4)+C$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x-4)^2+8(x-4)+16$",
          "worked": "Equating coefficients of $x^2$ gives $A=1$. Substitute $x=4$ to obtain $C$, then $x=5$ to obtain $B$.\n$$\\begin{align*}C&=4^2\\\\C&=16\\\\25&=1+B+16\\\\B&=8\\\\x^2&=(x-4)^2+8(x-4)+16\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p19-q7-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$A(x+2)^2+B(x+2)+C$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x+2)^2-4(x+2)+4$",
          "worked": "Equating coefficients of $x^2$ gives $A=1$. Substitute $x=-2$ to obtain $C$, then $x=-1$ to obtain $B$.\n$$\\begin{align*}C&=(-2)^2\\\\C&=4\\\\1&=1+B+4\\\\B&=-4\\\\x^2&=(x+2)^2-4(x+2)+4\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
